  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- **`TryGetForUpdate` holds the id's lock on MySQL also when it finds no taggregate,** as on SQL Server and PostgreSQL: no other unit of work adds a taggregate with that id until this one completes, so a get-or-create is safe. Before, both units of work went on, and the second to add the taggregate failed on the duplicate version. The lock is a row in a new table, `TaggregateLock`, which the store creates with the rest of its schema, and which keeps a row for every taggregate ever got for update.\n- **Internal support for Compze.Teventive.TeventStore's deleted taggregates; nothing public changes:** the store reads the type of each taggregate's last tevent, to tell the histories that end with an `ITaggregateDeletedTevent`. An application that upgrades Compze.Teventive.TeventStore to 0.7.0-alpha must upgrade this package too: the earlier version fails against it at runtime.\n- **Requires newer minor versions of other Compze packages:** Compze.Sql.MySql 0.6.0-alpha (was 0.5.0-alpha), Compze.Teventive.TeventStore.Abstractions 0.7.0-alpha (was 0.6.0-alpha). Upgrading to this version upgrades each package listed here too, so their changelogs apply to this upgrade as well.",
